#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:7 6e9c64b6c32d4d43aa9bbffe91fc4394
msgid "Multi-factor authentication within particular qubes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:10 6df2e931cabc4ca4b7c706809b14f159
msgid ""
"Most use cases for the hardware tokens can be achieved exactly as described "
"by the manufacturer or other instructions found online. One usually just "
"needs to attach the token (e.g. YubiKey) to the corresponding app qube to "
"get the same result (see the documentation on how to use :doc:`USB devices </"
"user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-usb-devices>` in Qubes OS accordingly). The "
"recommended way for using CTAP in Qubes is described :doc:`here </user/"
"security-in-qubes/ctap-proxy>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:13 7f0505d7ce45474fad5bab5bdb1a09f7
msgid "Multi-factor login for Qubes OS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:16 db050438ddc74e48a8b4d2a83db1bd49
msgid ""
"By default Qubes has two protection mechanisms against attackers. The first "
"is full disk encryption and the second the user login screen / lockscreen. "
"This article section concerns only adding multi-factor authentication to the "
"second one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:19 0806dd28d5c04ded9b508796687796a2
msgid "Time-based One-time Password (TOTP)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:22 33f618bebf53465ab749138061181ea2
msgid ""
"As the name implies, this generates authentication code that is time-"
"dependent. You can save the TOTP secret in a mobile app like `FreeOTP "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FreeOTP>`__ and then use it as an additional "
"factor to login to your Qubes system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/security-in-qubes/mfa.rst:24 33d6347708124c56b82fbb4a195e542e
msgid "**Warning**: remember to keep backup access codes."
msgstr ""

